<%- include('partials/head') %>
<body class="ph-body">
  <%- include('partials/nav') %>

  <section class="ph-page-hero">
    <div class="ph-container">
      <div class="ph-eyebrow">Feature deep-dive</div>
      <h1 class="ph-page-title">A player built for serious listeners.</h1>
      <p class="ph-page-lede">Every control you wish other apps had — and none of the ones you don't.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ph-section">
    <div class="ph-container ph-feature">
      <div class="ph-feature-copy">
        <h2>An expandable Play Bar.</h2>
        <p>The Play Bar floats inline as you browse, then expands into a full-screen sheet with artwork, fine-grained scrubbing, and access to every control. Tap the album art in the inline bar to jump straight to the episode detail. Tap the chevron-up to open the sheet.</p>
        <p>Optional: the bar can <strong>shrink as you scroll down</strong> a list, returning the screen real estate to the content. Re-opens with a scroll up.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="ph-feature-shot">
        <div class="ph-phone">
          <div class="ph-phone-screen">
            <img src="/public/images/podhaven/playbar-expanded.png" alt="The expanded Play Bar sheet over Up Next, showing artwork, scrubber, skip-back / pause / skip-forward, playback speed, and chapter controls." loading="lazy">
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ph-section ph-section-alt">
    <div class="ph-container">
      <h2 class="ph-section-title">Skip exactly how far you want.</h2>
      <p class="ph-lede">Forward and backward intervals are independent. Pick anywhere from <strong>5 to 90 seconds</strong> for each. Then those intervals apply <em>everywhere</em> — in-app buttons, lock screen, CarPlay, AirPods, Apple Watch, hardware skip buttons.</p>
      <div class="ph-grid">
        <div class="ph-card">
          <h3>Skip Forward Interval</h3>
          <p>Default 30s. Step in 5-second increments. Bigger number = catch up faster.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ph-card">
          <h3>Skip Backward Interval</h3>
          <p>Default 15s. Smaller is better here — you usually only need to re-hear the last sentence.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ph-card">
          <h3>Hardware buttons too</h3>
          <p>Your AirPods squeeze, lock-screen controls, and car steering-wheel buttons all use these intervals. One setting, every playback surface.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ph-section">
    <div class="ph-container ph-feature ph-feature-flip">
      <div class="ph-feature-copy">
        <h2>Undo Seek — for when your thumb slips.</h2>
        <p>Scrubbed too far? Toggle <em>Enable Undo Seek</em> in Settings. Now any time you drag the progress bar, the skip-backward button briefly transforms into an <strong>Undo</strong> button. Tap once to jump back to your previous position.</p>
        <p>It's the kind of small affordance you'll forget you turned on, until the day you accidentally palm the screen on a bumpy commute.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="ph-feature-shot">
        <div class="ph-phone">
          <div class="ph-phone-screen">
            <img src="/public/images/podhaven/settings-playback.png" alt="Settings showing Default Playback Rate, Next Track Behavior, Skip Forward 30s, Skip Backward 15s, and Enable Undo Seek toggle." loading="lazy">
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ph-section ph-section-alt">
    <div class="ph-container">
      <h2 class="ph-section-title">Speed, chapters, and Next Track behavior.</h2>
      <ul class="ph-checklist ph-checklist-wide">
        <li><strong>Playback speed 0.8× – 2.0×</strong> in 0.1× increments. The default applies to new episodes; per-episode tweaks stick to that episode.</li>
        <li><strong>Chapter navigation.</strong> Episodes with embedded chapters get prev/next chapter buttons in the expanded Play Bar.</li>
        <li><strong>Lock-screen Next behavior</strong> is configurable: jump to the next queued episode, skip by your interval, or move to the next chapter (when one exists). Pick the one your hands expect.</li>
        <li><strong>System audio output.</strong> Because PodHaven uses iOS long-form audio, playback works with the same AirPlay, Bluetooth, CarPlay, and route controls you use for other audio apps.</li>
        <li><strong>Command Center scrubbing</strong> is on by default — drag the progress bar right from the lock screen, Control Center, or CarPlay. Prone to bumping it? Turn it off in Settings and the skip buttons and progress display stay put.</li>
        <li><strong>Per-podcast playback rate override.</strong> The fast-talker show can run at 1.0× while everything else stays at 1.4×. Set it from the per-podcast settings sheet. <a class="ph-inline-link" href="/podhaven/guides/per-podcast-settings#playback-rate">How to →</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ph-section">
    <div class="ph-container">
      <h2 class="ph-section-title">Lock-screen, CarPlay, and Watch in sync.</h2>
      <p class="ph-lede">PodHaven uses iOS's long-form audio session and the system Now Playing info, so the lock screen, Control Center, CarPlay, AirPods squeeze, and Apple Watch playback controls all reflect the same playhead and the same artwork.</p>
      <p>Pause on your phone, resume on CarPlay, finish on AirPods. The position is synced through the system, so there's no "wait a sec, where was I?" beat.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%- include('partials/footer') %>
